# Terraform state — may contain plaintext secret values; local-only.
**/.terraform/
**/.terraform.lock.hcl
**/terraform.tfstate
**/terraform.tfstate.backup
**/tfplan*.binary

# tfvars are sensitive — deployment-specific config (project IDs, URLs,
# regions, naming) changes per deployment and is NOT committed; the repo is
# cloned by many people. Commit ONLY the .example templates.
*.tfvars
!*.tfvars.example

# Real deployments live here — never committed. examples/ holds the templates
# you copy FROM; env/<name>/ is where you fill real values + hold state.
/env/

# GCP service-account key files. Broad rule + anchored defense-in-depth so a
# real key stays ignored even if *.json is ever narrowed.
*.json
/*-*.json
**/*-sa.json
**/sa-*.json

# SSH private keys generated by an apply. env/ is already ignored whole, so this
# is the defense for an apply run from examples/ by mistake — the key would
# otherwise land in a committed directory with nothing stopping it.
**/netbird-id
**/id_ed25519*
**/id_rsa*
*.pem
